codex
The per-label diagnostic exposed an important proof-structure detail: selecting one loop claim removes the sibling circularities it relies on at digit/slash phase transitions, so the prover keeps unrolling the symbolic tail. I’m stopping that diagnostic and will run the complete seven-claim module together, which is the correct independent reconstruction of this mutually recursive invariant family.
